          "tree_id": "5f9b591479da3027855dd9b36cf322f2d240a6a9",
          "message": "release: 1.7.0 — do not merge until Sean publishes Friday (#558)\n\n* release: 1.7.0 (WIP) — version, CHANGELOG, since-1.7.0 labels, site install strings, harness live/direction\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* release: 1.7.0 — quarantine CHANGELOG (with #557), 105-file tarball, remaining install pins\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* release: 1.7.0 — every CHANGELOG line names the code or test that makes it true\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* release: 1.7.0 — CHANGELOG matches #557 round 2 (grounded, no SDK HAL transport, --trusted screened)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* release: 1.7.0 — CHANGELOG lines for #556 (arithmetic-approx) and #554 (extension parity, not in the tarball)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(memory): a grounded release never prints VERIFIED; --help names the default backend for --check hal\n\nXC1 S3 items on #557:\n- The ground release's released_by said \"(VERIFIED <reason> page N)\",\n  the quote check's status, so a grounded row printed the word VERIFIED.\n  It now says \"(quote found: <reason>, page N)\"; \"verified\" appears only\n  for HAL releases.\n- CLI --help says --check hal asks the default backend only, as the\n  README and api-reference egress tables do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* release: 1.7.0 — quarantine labels read \"since 1.7.0\"; CHANGELOG dated 2026-10-16\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* release: 1.7.0 — the two remaining --version pins read 1.7\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* release: 1.7.0 — the 2^53 edge says what the tests show (a JS number is not checked; the same digits as a string verify)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* release: 1.7.0 — CHANGELOG line for #564 (check drops the NVIDIA NIM and Z.ai display names)\n\nRebased onto main 583c1d81. The only package change main gained since this\nbranch was cut is #564's VOTER_NAMES edit in src/lib/claim.ts and\ndist/lib/claim.js; both are now byte-identical to main. A fresh sdk:build\nmatches the committed dist (line endings only).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* release: 1.7.0 — re-cut on main 51897d4c: CHANGELOG for #571-#575 and #577, 107-file tarball\n\nRebased onto main 51897d4c (#571, #572, #573, #574, #575, #577). The README\nMCP paragraph conflict is resolved to main's content in 1.7.0 voice: no MCP\nredact, network-read tools answer {untrusted_data, screening}.\n\nCHANGELOG 1.7.0:\n- #573 is a BEHAVIOR CHANGE for MCP consumers: network-read tool results are\n  {untrusted_data, screening}; an agent reading `verdict` must read\n  `untrusted_data.verdict`. The MCP redact tool is removed.\n- #572 OFFLINE=1 sends nothing; #574 TRUSTSHELL_API_URL is https only;\n  #575 memory folder 0700 / file 0600.\n- #571 (extension first-run opt-in) and #577 (site UX) are named as not in\n  the npm tarball.\n- Package size: 107 files (dist/lib/api-url.js and .d.ts are new).\n\n#576 (localOnly) is not in 1.7.0. A fresh sdk:build matches the committed\ndist (line endings only).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: name the learn MCP tools where the README tool list is read\n\nThe check compared the names between \"its tools are\" and \"It has no\npurchase tool\" with the tools the server registers. learn_lessons_for\nand learn_record were registered and sat after that sentence.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
